        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start the process at the Italian restaurant, first enter and ask for the menu."
      ],
      "justification": "Implicitly starts the process and directly captures the first action step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After checking the offers"
      ],
      "justification": "A temporal phrasing re-typed as an action step; preserves the intended sequence and behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "simultaneously take the following steps: order a glass of red wine and a salad."
      ],
      "justification": "Parallel instructions split into two discrete action nodes; simultaneous behaviour is preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the order is placed, wait for it to arrive and then enjoy the salad and wine."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly covers the waiting and consumption phases described in the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After finishing, you will be asked if you would like a dessert."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the dessert inquiry step and opens the XOR decision gateway for the answer."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you answer \"yes\" to tiramisu, then go ahead and order it."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the positive response condition and the subsequent ordering action; value/threshold semantics preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you answer \"no\" to tiramisu, then simply decline any dessert."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the negative response condition and the subsequent declining action; logic preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you did order tiramisu, wait for it to be served, then enjoy it."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the conditional waiting and enjoyment steps for the dessert branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once you are ready, ask for the bill and proceed to pay it."
      ],
      "justification": "Splits the billing instruction into two sequential action steps without changing behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After settling the bill, you can leave the restaurant and the process will be complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers departure, completion statement, and process termination. Redundant restatement of completion does not alter behaviour."
    }
